#: ../../source/timsort_README.md:6
msgid ""
"An adaptive and **stable** sort algorithm based on merging that requires "
"fewer than nlog(n)  comparisons when run on partially sorted arrays. The "
"algorithm uses O(n) memory and still runs in O(nlogn)  (worst case) on "
"random arrays.   This implementation is based on the original  "
"[TimSort](http://svn.python.org/projects/python/trunk/Objects/listsort.txt)"
" developed  by Tim Peters for Python's lists (code "
"[here](http://svn.python.org/projects/python/trunk/Objects/listobject.c))."
" TimSort has been also adopted in Java starting from version 7."
msgstr ""

